WEBVTT

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.270
Congratulations, Graduates

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.080
Ren!

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.890
Since it's our last day, 
let's go out to eat together.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.400
I have to pack.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.820
I heard about that, but it's our graduation.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.270
And all the girls are after your e-mail address, 
thinking this is their last chance.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.640
Mine? Why?

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.310
A transfer student raised 
abroad attracts attention.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.490
On top of that, your brother 
is a host with a showy face.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.940
You think they'll just ignore such 
an appealing pair of brother?

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.630
I don't understand.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.530
Okay, forget it.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.040
But you'd better come next time.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.930
Fine.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.670
Later.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.240
<i>I don't understand Japanese people.</i>

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.130
Ren!

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.760
Found you!

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.930
I've been looking for you.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.510
You weren't in your classroom, 
and then I got held up by some moms,

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.510
so I pretended I didn't speak any Japanese.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.720
Aren't you used to that kind of 
thing from working as a host?

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.920
My customers and ordinary 
women just aren't the same.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:11.940
So, how was graduation? Sad?

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.050
Not really.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.070
I was there less than six months.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.760
I never even learned the faces 
of most of my classmates.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.190
And having to start school 
again so soon is depressing.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:26.270
You learned all the dogs' faces 
right away! What's wrong with you?

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.350
Oh, right. We need to stop 
by a Japanese sweets shop.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:33.980
My landlord asked me to pick 
up some strawberry daifuku.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.510
Strawberry daifuku?

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:13.810
Why did he buy so many groceries 
when he's moving tomorrow?

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.610
To celebrate his graduation.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.500
Ren apparently doesn't like eating out.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.830
Well, I'm having meat!

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.140
You should eat some vegetables, too.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.620
Shut up.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:28.140
Haru

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:28.140
Clothes

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:28.140
Trinkets

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.140
Besides, this will be his last
night in this apartment.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.230
It must be emotional for him.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.860
You think so?

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.610
We're back.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:38.870
Welcome home. How was 
the graduation ceremony?

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.200
Nothing special...

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.370
I got held up by a bunch of moms.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:48.070
<i>Starting tomorrow, the four of us 
will be living together in our new home.</i>

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.580
Man, time flies.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:56.040
He's already graduated, but it hasn't even 
been six months since he started school.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.930
Well, we came back to Japan in October, so...

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:03.110
You should've brought him back immediately!

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:06.670
Why'd you have to lounge around in 
the Canadian countryside for so long?

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:11.060
I'm surprised Ren agreed 
to live in Japan, though.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.560
Well, for a long time, he wouldn't.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.650
My visa was about to run out, too...

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.590
Oh, my. It's nearly new rice reason in Japan.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.570
New rice?

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.180
It means the freshly 
harvested rice of that year.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.580
It's plump and shiny when freshly 
cooked, and it's absolutely delicious.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:36.260
Come to think of it, you've never 
had new rice before, have you?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.590
Door to the Unknown

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.330
What? That's why he came back?

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:45.820
He made me go buy new rice 
the second we got home...

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.590
He even wanted a particular brand.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.850
When I asked him what he wanted for 
Christmas last year, he said a rice cooker!

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.230
And what kind of three-cup 
rice cooker costs 150,000 yen?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.560
You still went and bought it right away.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.870
Yeah, but...

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.280
Onodera

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.280
You're so selfish!

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.290
You're not my problem anymore!

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:10.560
Gramps?

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.370
Eh?

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.410
Oh, it's you.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.610
Was she your guest?

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.610
That's Setsuko, my son's evil wife.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.410
Strawberry daifuku.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:22.810
Ah, perfect timing. 
Come on in and have some tea.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.920
Whole 
Strawberry

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.260
I didn't know you had a son.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.640
It's been five years since he died of cancer.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.930
His wife won't shut up about selling the 
apartment building and getting a condo.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:38.150
That building <i>is</i> pretty old.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.540
If you don't like it, move out!

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.940
Wait, you're moving out tomorrow, aren't you?

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:48.660
Come to think of it, he's my oldest tenant.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.580
At first, I thought he was a real gaudy kid,

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.850
but he said he wanted to live 
with his brothers someday.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:01.050
He never failed to pay his rent, 
and he always worked hard.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.650
Gramps, what are you doing?

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:11.720
A raccoon dog's been living under 
my house since about a week ago.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.100
A raccoon dog?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.230
You've never seen one before?

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.350
There are a lot of raccoons in Vancouver...

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:23.310
Well, they're similar.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.860
He'll be my only roommate for a while.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.660
I should get going.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.210
I need to pack.

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:37.430
Ren, you don't seem

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:43.880
the slightest bit happy about moving 
in with your brothers tomorrow.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.250
I don't mind it.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.420
I just...

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.390
It's fine.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.770
If you don't like your stupid brother, 
you can come back here anytime.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.140
This old man will listen to your complaints.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.620
And when you do, bring some 
three-color yokan with you.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:08.770
<i>He wanted to live with his brothers someday...</i>

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:13.060
<i>So he's been saying that for a long time.</i>

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:18.800
Haru?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:23.250
Ren, what's up? We have 
to be up early tomorrow.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.380
Aki's going to crush me in his sleep.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.260
Whump

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.260
Thud

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.260
That must've been rough.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:33.150
You can sleep with me on 
the sofa bed, if you want.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.760
Do you need any help?

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.040
Nah, I'm already finished.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:38.770
I see.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.020
Wha... Ren?

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:45.260
Hey, what's wrong?

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.700
Why do you ask?

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:52.030
Do you not like that I decided 
to move without consulting you?

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.780
It wasn't my decision to make.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:58.310
Then you don't want to live with Aki and Shima?

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.740
I just...

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:01.410
Just what?

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:05.880
I think Aki and Shima are the 
ones who aren't happy with it.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.830
I practically kept you all
to myself the past year.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.550
If I were them,

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.800
I don't think I'd like that at all.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:22.310
<i>I thought he'd gotten somewhat used to me,</i>

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.260
<i>after we lived together for a year.</i>

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:30.000
<i>But he never shows or says how he feels,</i>

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.320
<i>so sometimes I start to forget...</i>

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:34.320
Ren.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:39.080
<i>I really am loved.</i>

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.110
Ha—

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:43.710
Ow!

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.750
You're such a pest!

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.970
<i>Normally, I'm not confident 
about that at all, though.</i>

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.340
Natsu-san!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.930
I'm here to help you move!

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.920
Wow!

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.160
You found a pretty nice place to live.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.860
I'm renting it really cheap from Mikiko-san.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:10.840
Do lawyers make that much money?

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.540
Her family is wealthy to begin with.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.020
I'm so jealous.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.610
My family are all farmers.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:19.930
My parents, my sister's husband's 
family, and even both my brothers!

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.490
They're all farmers!

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:22.620
So here!

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:26.040
I got you fresh vegetables 
to celebrate your move!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.130
Thanks for going to the trouble.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.380
Hey, it's Iku.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.410
It's good to see you again, Ikuyoshi-san.

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:33.630
Hey!

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.340
I thought maybe I could help out somehow.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.650
You're too late.

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:40.140
Really?

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:43.090
Ren, is all your stuff in your room?

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.500
I'm already unpacked.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.100
Ren Ren, you're as unfriendly as—
I mean, as cool as ever.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:53.000
Being friendly to you wouldn't 
benefit him in any way.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.220
In fact, it'd be bad for him.

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.150
He's blinded by love...

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:59.290
Bro, are you turning the other building

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.120
into a storage shed or something?

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:05.770
Yeah, I'm thinking of quitting 
as a host and opening a store.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:09.420
And that's where I'll come in handy!

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:10.540
Huh?

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:19.800
Ah, Haru. It's unusual to see 
you out of your host suit.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.000
This is actually how I normally dress.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.560
So, how's the house?

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.060
We're mostly unpacked. It's comfortable.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.540
What's wrong?

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:35.070
You're finally getting to live 
with all your brothers,

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.480
but you seem down.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:39.310
Nah, everything's going too well, really.

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:41.100
You're right.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:44.030
You're getting to live with your twin brothers,

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:47.640
and Ren has even been offered scholarships.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.570
He is smart.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:56.050
Then why are you so worried?

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.460
Well... I think I may have rushed the move.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:02.540
Is it Ren?

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.800
Is he not used to living with the twins yet?

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.810
No, it's not like that.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.370
How can I put it?

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.630
In the old apartment, 
we slept in the same room.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:17.790
No matter what we did, we were always 
close enough to sense each other.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:19.700
But in the house...

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:21.870
What does Ren say?

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.150
Nothing.

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:26.580
But he's been staying cooped up 
in his room since we moved...

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.270
And lately, I've been busy, too...

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:32.690
Why don't you get a dog? 
He likes them, right?

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:36.670
When he says "dogs," he means 
wolves that weigh 50 kilos!

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.590
There's no way!

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:39.050
You know...

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:42.110
You're such an overprotective brother.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.140
Normally, boys Ren's age find it annoying

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:46.850
when their parents and siblings 
meddle with their lives.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.600
Gasp!! 
Aki said the same 
thing to me once!!

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.590
What? No way!

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:49.600
I'm annoying?

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:51.900
Yeah.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.480
Actually, that sounds 
like something he'd say.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:56.480
But...

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:01.020
He was so moved by your kindness,
he came all the way from Canada for you.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:04.040
He must like you quite a bit.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:06.350
Hey, Ren!

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.240
Ren, are you here?

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:09.360
What?

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.360
Say something if you're here.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.500
You've been cooped up in your room.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.320
Look, I rented a DVD.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.850
Let's watch it downstairs.

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:19.510
Where's Shima?

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.010
At work.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:24.670
Bro asked me to take care 
of you until he comes back.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:27.600
And I don't have time, either. Come on.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:29.560
It's okay.

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:30.820
Huh?

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:32.850
You can ignore me.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:34.600
I'm fine.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:38.360
We live together. I can't do that.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.020
I'm trying to be considerate here.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.860
Why do you need to be considerate?

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.410
Because Bro brought you here!

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.720
Jeez, you're such a pain in the ass.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.320
I don't want to take care of you, either.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:57.850
Having another younger 
brother is annoying enough.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:59.620
If you just wanted to be ignored,

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:02.880
you should've told Bro that 
when he went to get you!

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.880
You're just a brat who can't 
do anything by himself.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.350
Quit making adults do everything for you.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:11.590
<i>A brat?</i>

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.290
<i>I realize that more than I'd like to admit.</i>

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:20.020
Huh?

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.580
Ren, you're alone? Where's Aki?

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:23.990
He went to work.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.650
Shima's at work, too.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:30.030
It'll finally be just the two 
of us for dinner again.

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:31.430
Haru.

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:34.750
I want to work, too.

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:36.970
You want to do what?

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:38.100
Work.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.000
Who does?

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:39.920
I do.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.380
Okay, peel these, then.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.760
When you're finished, 
peel the daikon and carrots, too.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:49.760
Tonight's dinner is pork soup 
and fish boiled in soy sauce.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.260
Skin?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.260
Skin?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.260
Skin?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.260
Skin?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.260
Remaining Potato

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.260
That's not what I meant by work!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:56.270
Sure it is! You think life is easy?

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:59.550
Your language is impolite, 
you can't manage a friendly smile,

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:01.650
and you can't even peel a potato properly!

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:05.750
No one's going to hire 
an awkward kid like you!

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.150
Or what?

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:08.910
Is it money that you want?

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.080
Aki and Shima have jobs.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.630
They're just trying to earn some pocket money.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:20.550
But shouldn't I cover my own living expenses?

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:23.780
Is that what you're worried about?

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:25.050
No.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:30.260
My littlest brother might 
be the biggest worrywart.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.510
Stop treating me like a child!

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:34.100
It's fine.

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:37.610
You can be a kid for a while longer.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.170
If you grow up too fast,

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.690
you won't need me anymore.

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:49.430
I'm not staying with you because I'm a child.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.590
Really?

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:55.240
Then I hope you'll say that 
next year and the year after.

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:57.390
I'll never stop needing you.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.400
I see...

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.960
<i>Even at his age, this childlike adult</i>

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:07.520
<i>is more of a baby than I am.</i>

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.170
<i>It's not good.</i>

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:17.390
Gramps, are you out?

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:21.080
Gramps!

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.320
Sheesh! I can't believe you broke 
your leg falling from the veranda!

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:33.070
Sulk

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:33.070
I'm always telling you to be 
careful since you're old now!

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:37.830
Sulk

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:36.700
What would've happened 
if this boy hadn't found you?

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.350
Naturally, you'll be staying 
in the hospital for a few days!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.040
She's the lady from the other day.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:48.520
That evil woman is the head nurse here.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:53.150
But it's true that I caused you 
trouble with all this.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.260
It's fine.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.060
I just stopped by because I was free.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.100
Is that so?

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.170
Since I've already troubled you, 
could you do something else for me?

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:01.700
At my house—

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:02.630
Is it the raccoon dog?

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:06.080
Yeah, look after him for me.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:11.050
You probably came to complain 
about your stupid brother,

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:15.620
but while I'm gone, you can distract 
yourself by cleaning the place.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:16.870
You are free, right?

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.330
Right?

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.330
Great, thanks.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:24.790
Bro!

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:28.770
What happened? I heard Ren 
got hurt and is at the hospital!

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:29.790
Was it an accident?

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.550
Or...

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:36.580
How can you two be so calm?

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:38.070
I see.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:41.310
That's what you assumed since you 
hung up before I was finished.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.310
Huh?

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:46.860
My former landlord is the one who's
in the hospital with a broken leg.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:48.610
Ren happened to find him.

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:50.570
Huh?

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:50.570
Huh...?

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.390
Why are you so flustered?

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.420
Did you do something to Ren that 
you're feeling guilty about now?

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.070
N-No...

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.340
I didn't...

00:16:58.370 --> 00:16:59.580
I said something, though...

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:02.460
Then go pick up Ren.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.790
He's at the old man's place.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.590
I have to get to work.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.230
Bro, you're really going to quit being a host?

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:14.470
I told you before. I'm opening a store.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:16.970
Is it for Ren?

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:22.430
I think I was just pretending 
to care about you guys

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:25.920
when, really, I was only thinking of myself.

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.640
I came back to Japan

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:34.450
because Ren helped me decide 
it would be best for us, too.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.890
But that's...

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:40.330
He suddenly announced yesterday

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.950
that he wants to work, too.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.940
He wants to cover his own living expenses.

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.700
It's funny, right?

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:52.200
He can't even get through 
an automatic ticket gate,

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.720
and he's overwhelmed by crowds.

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:58.650
When I was his age,

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:00.970
all I thought about was dumb stuff.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.230
So don't let him outdo you, too,

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.750
big brother.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:14.080
<i>Our brother four years our senior 
seemed like a great man to us.</i>

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.490
<i>He still does.</i>

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.440
I wondered why you weren't back yet.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:21.400
What are you doing?

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:21.990
Aki...

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:25.840
The old man asked me to clean 
his house while he's gone.

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:27.500
That old man...

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.920
Well, whatever. I bought dinners. Let's eat.

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:33.470
Which one do you want?

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:34.760
Either.

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:37.350
Then I'm taking the fried chicken.

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:43.440
I heard you told Bro you want to work.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.120
Yeah...

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:45.680
Why?

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.640
Haru isn't obligated to take care of me.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:53.150
He'd cry if he heard you say that.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:58.540
Haru's dream was to someday 
live with all his brothers.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.900
And that has come true.

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.590
With all his brothers.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.710
I'm an outsider.

00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:11.420
When I first came to Japan,

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.860
I was happy just seeing Haru's face.

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:18.000
I'd always wanted to see him again...

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:22.070
But I didn't know I was on 
the Kaidou family register.

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:23.440
What? Seriously?

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:24.220
Yeah.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:27.190
In the end,

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:30.230
I upset you and Haru by being here.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:32.640
Haru's nice.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:36.940
When I'm around him, I feel 
like the kid I was when we met.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:42.000
What's wrong with that?

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:45.570
If we weren't around, that turd

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:49.580
would probably have been snagged by some 
woman and be living an aimless life.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:54.100
None of the women who swarm 
around him have ever been any good.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.590
I know that.

00:19:56.190 --> 00:20:00.420
And Shima and I are probably the same.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:04.180
Aki, you broke up with your girlfriend again?

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:08.280
Well, she kept asking about Bro!

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:12.350
And you've never had any 
long-term relationships, either!

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:15.870
Because you always interfere with mine.

00:20:15.870 --> 00:20:18.610
That's because she was two-timing you!

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:20.670
Actually, it was three.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:22.050
It's fine, though.

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.470
We both knew.

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:24.740
You're the worst!

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:31.250
Brothers Who Have 
Terrible Luck with Women

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:28.850
Just thinking about it makes me want to cry.

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:31.250
Sorry. I don't get it.

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:33.160
You don't have to.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:35.620
In fact, I hope you never do.

00:20:37.490 --> 00:20:39.760
Actually, since you showed up,

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:41.720
we haven't had time to think about it.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:45.420
Now that I think about it, 
we've been living decent lives lately.

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:48.530
So it's good having a kid like you around.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:53.790
With you here, Bro won't 
bring women home, either.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:57.270
It's better for guys like him 
to have kids like you around.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.270
Really?

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:03.780
Buying a 150,000 yen rice cooker 
for you seems stupid,

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:08.780
but as much as he's been provided for, 
he's never provided for someone else.

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:12.790
Serves him right! It's so funny...

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:23.580
I forgot to feed him.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.180
Huh?

00:21:27.860 --> 00:21:30.540
Brother, you're alone? Where's Ren?

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:31.990
Seeing the old man.

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:34.000
Oh, yeah. He got out of the hospital, right?

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.190
He forced them to let him go.

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:38.440
He said something about having 
to take care of a raccoon dog...

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:39.990
A raccoon dog?

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:43.940
Come to think of it, 
Aki sent me a picture of one...

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:45.450
Aki 
Found a raccoon dog!!

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:45.450
Isn't this cool?

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:50.080
This isn't a raccoon dog...

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:51.750
Isn't that a Pomeranian?

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:53.580
Yep.

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:57.040
It was definitely a raccoon 
dog living under my house.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.150
I see. So this is a raccoon dog.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.960
Both have no idea 
what Pomeranians are.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:40.100
Next Time
